{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKizwUSdgNd1usRhZ4UT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `.ard/157/review-eng-review.md` with a verdict of **changes**, based on one blocking medium finding.\n\nThe change fixes the non-lead path correctly. Non-lead claims on admitted human issues now log `admitted`, and App-authored issues still log `app-authored`. Both cases have new subtests.\n\nThe problem is in the lead role's path. It now passes through `consider` with no reason set. A lead claim on a human issue with an unchanged stored admission goes through `gate`, which returns a nil record there, so the claim logs `reason=` empty. That is the same kind of misleading audit log the issue describes. The fix is to set `ReasonAdmitted` in that case too, and to add a lead-role test for it.\n\nI ran `go test ./internal/triage/... ./internal/intake/...`, which passed, and `go vet` on both packages, which was clean. I did not run a separate coverage report. The lead matching-admission branch has no test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":737,"cache_read_input_tokens":18960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":737},"output_tokens":313,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6bbea3d-e578-4599-b5af-ddf6c7a3a475","uuid":"2196628c-826c-4dcc-9c51-1a842ba2a5ca","timestamp":"2026-11-23T10:45:50.438Z","request_id":"req_011ChKizwLG7pEdYiKJd49Nr"}
